Subject: [PATCH] Fix a crash when a queued item changes while the queue window opens

The download queue window registers as a QueueManager listener and only
then takes its snapshot of the queue under the queue lock. Events fired in
between are delivered asynchronously, after the snapshot that already
reflects them. When an item is updated and then removed in that gap (for
example a file list that finishes downloading while the window opens, or
while it waits for the queue lock), the window never lists the item, and
the queued update dereferences the null QueueItemInfo returned by
getItemInfo in onUpdated:

  QueueItem.h setPriority <- QueueFrame::onUpdated <- Application::dispatch

An item added in the same gap is also listed twice.

Register the listener inside lockedOperation, so the snapshot and the
subscription happen in one step. QueueManager fires its events with the
queue lock held (FileMoved, fired from the file mover thread, has no
listener that takes the queue lock), so the lock order is the same as in
fire() itself. Also ignore an update for an item the window doesn't list,
as onRemoved already does, and free the update's copy on every path.

Applies to the standard DC++ 0.884 source tree.

diff --git a/win32/QueueFrame.cpp b/win32/QueueFrame.cpp
--- a/win32/QueueFrame.cpp
+++ b/win32/QueueFrame.cpp
@@ -161,8 +161,13 @@
 
 	setTimer([this]() -> bool { updateStatus(); return true; }, 500);
 
-	QueueManager::getInstance()->addListener(this);
-	QueueManager::getInstance()->lockedOperation([this](const QueueItem::StringMap& qsm) { addQueueList(qsm); });
+	// Listen and read the queue in one locked step. An event fired in between would otherwise
+	// reach this window after a snapshot that already has its effect: the update of an item
+	// removed meanwhile then found no row, and an item added meanwhile was listed twice.
+	QueueManager::getInstance()->lockedOperation([this](const QueueItem::StringMap& qsm) {
+		QueueManager::getInstance()->addListener(this);
+		addQueueList(qsm);
+	});
 
 	layout();
 }
@@ -1139,7 +1144,12 @@
 }
 
 void QueueFrame::onUpdated(QueueItem* qi) {
+	unique_ptr<QueueItem> copy(qi);
 	QueueItemInfo* ii = getItemInfo(qi->getTarget());
+	if(!ii) {
+		// Not listed here (as onRemoved); there is nothing to update.
+		return;
+	}
 
 	ii->setPriority(qi->getPriority());
 	ii->setStatus(QueueItemInfo::getStatus(*qi));
@@ -1154,8 +1164,6 @@
 		ii->update();
 		files->update(ii);
 	}
-
-	delete qi;
 }
 
 void QueueFrame::onRechecked(const string& target, const tstring& message) {
